{
  "name": "StreamVault: post Shorts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## StreamVault: post the next Short\n\nRuns every 4 hours. Looks at every folder in **OneDrive/StreamVault/ready/**, skips Shorts on hold, and picks the highest priority (set in the StreamVault app), then the best score, then the oldest. Uploads its video.mp4 to YouTube with the title, description and tags from post.json, writes result.json next to it and moves the folder to **posted/**.\n\n**Uploader** (top of *Build upload*): `'browser'` dispatches the GitHub workflow that uploads through YouTube Studio and waits up to 45 min for its report; `'api'` uses the YouTube Data API (needs Google's audit for public videos).\n\nNothing waiting = nothing happens. A run that fails (signed out, upload limit, Studio changed) leaves the Short in ready/ and shows red in Executions; a Short that fails itself (copyright) or never gets a report gets a result.json and is skipped from then on. Screenshots of failures go to **failures/**.\n\n**Change how often:** open *Every 4 hours* and edit the cron (minute hour …).\n**Privacy, category, language:** top of *Build upload*.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 560
      },
      "id": "899b9507-c1d4-53d2-859c-3089703d78cd",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -220,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 */4 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "4e815419-6de1-5cb9-b023-9c7839d493b7",
      "name": "Every 4 hours",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
